usage: train.py [-h] --data-root DATA_ROOT [--output-dir OUTPUT_DIR]
                [--device DEVICE] [--architecture ARCHITECTURE]
                [--encoder-name ENCODER_NAME]
                [--encoder-weights ENCODER_WEIGHTS] [--patch-size PATCH_SIZE]
                [--input-scale INPUT_SCALE]
                [--samples-per-image SAMPLES_PER_IMAGE]
                [--batch-size BATCH_SIZE]
                [--accumulation-steps ACCUMULATION_STEPS]
                [--num-workers NUM_WORKERS] [--epochs EPOCHS] [--lr LR]
                [--encoder-lr-mult ENCODER_LR_MULT]
                [--weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY]
                [--ce-class-weights AL AL3NI PRIMARY_SI EUTECTIC_SI]
                [--init-checkpoint INIT_CHECKPOINT] [--no-boundary-head]
                [--boundary-head-weight BOUNDARY_HEAD_WEIGHT] [--seed SEED]
                [--val-every VAL_EVERY] [--no-amp] [--resume]

Train the phase-segmentation model (defaults = the released best recipe).

UNet++ + HRNet-W48 (ImageNet), 512 patches cut from 256 native px (input
scale 2), CE + Dice without class weights, plus a training-only
class-agnostic boundary head. The final model is `<output-dir>/last.pt`.

The per-epoch validation printed here is only a quick progress signal: each
valid image goes through the model in one padded pass at native scale,
which doesn't match input_scale=2 training, so its numbers run well below
the real metric. Use evaluate.py (overlap-tile, same as prediction) for
the actual mIoU.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --data-root DATA_ROOT
                        Folder with train/ and valid/ (see README).
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --device DEVICE
  --architecture ARCHITECTURE
  --encoder-name ENCODER_NAME
  --encoder-weights ENCODER_WEIGHTS
  --patch-size PATCH_SIZE
  --input-scale INPUT_SCALE
                        Must match at evaluate/predict time.
  --samples-per-image SAMPLES_PER_IMAGE
  --batch-size BATCH_SIZE
  --accumulation-steps ACCUMULATION_STEPS
                        Micro-batches per optimizer update (use 4 with batch-
                        size 2 to keep effective batch 8).
  --num-workers NUM_WORKERS
  --epochs EPOCHS
  --lr LR
  --encoder-lr-mult ENCODER_LR_MULT
  --weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY
  --ce-class-weights AL AL3NI PRIMARY_SI EUTECTIC_SI
                        Optional weights for CE only, in the fixed class
                        order.
  --init-checkpoint INIT_CHECKPOINT
                        Initialize model weights from an inference checkpoint
                        and start a fresh optimizer.
  --no-boundary-head    Train without the boundary auxiliary head.
  --boundary-head-weight BOUNDARY_HEAD_WEIGHT
  --seed SEED
  --val-every VAL_EVERY
                        0 = no per-epoch validation.
  --no-amp              Disable CUDA FP16 autocast.
  --resume              Resume from output-dir/train_state.pt when present.
